    "case_id": "529",
    "case_summary": "A 50-year-old man presented with subjective fevers, shortness of breath, and worsening cough for 6 days. Medical history includes:- Common variable immunodeficiency (CVID) receiving intravenous immunoglobulin every 3 weeks- HIV with undetectable viral load, CD4 count 140 cells/µL on therapy- Chronic bronchiectasis with history of Mycobacterium avium complex pulmonary infection- Recurrent giardiasis- Myopathy (treated with long-term low-dose prednisone)- Recurrent herpes simplex virus infections14 months prior, the patient presented with pharyngitis. He was on trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole for Pneumocystis prophylaxis.\n\n- Oxygen saturation was 97% on room air- Developed bilateral lower-extremity edema- Ulceration of the glans penis noted during treatment course\n\nLaboratory Tests:- CD4 count: 140 cells/µL- HIV viral load: Undetectable- Viral resistance testing showed mutations in UL97 (C592G) and UL54 (N408K) genes- Serial CMV viral load measurements:  * 63 IU/mL (1 month after initial treatment)  * 1089 IU/mL  * 321 IU/mL  * 340 IU/mL  * 660 IU/mL  * 1660 IU/mL and 3171 IU/mL (during hospital admission)Imaging Studies:- CT scan of the chest  Image Description: Shows bronchiectasis with no consolidations or ground-glass opacitiesPathological Tests:- Pharyngeal biopsy (14 months prior)- Ophthalmologic examination showed no evidence of retinitis",
